:: Mansion Piano Fox
<<effects>><<summon_brown_fox 1>><<person1>>
You creep down the stairs, towards the lounge. Each footfall makes you nervous. You consider looking for something to use as a weapon, but there's a paradoxical sense of calm washing over you. Your fingers feel loose. You have no grip strength.
<br><br>

It's nostalgic, but you don't know why. As you get closer, your legs feel heavier. Your footsteps slow. The melody slows with them, each one playing when your foot hits the floor.
<br><br>

<<if $avery_fate is "ascended">>
	Then, you hear a <<personsimple>>'s gentle voice. Soothing like birdsong.
	<br><br>

	<<He>> sings.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Mansion Piano Demon]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Next|Mansion Piano Fox 2]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>


:: Mansion Piano Demon
<<effects>>
<span class="narration">
My dear child, please don't hide<br>
Beside the Elks, abide<br>
A return to the tide.<br><br>
</span>

You step into the lounge doorway. A beam of <<if Time.isBloodMoon()>>red<</if>> moonlight lands just below the piano, revealing the end of a dark green cloak.
<<if $avery_mansion.fox.known>>
	<span class="red">A brown fox mask lies cast aside on the floor.</span>
<<else>>
	A brown fox mask, nearly identical to the ones you've worn, lies cast aside on the floor.
<</if>>
<br><br>

<span class="narration">
Feel the salt on your skin,<br>
Whispered name on the wind,<br>
All the weight of our sin.<br><br>
</span>

The notes of the final word are much louder. It shakes you to your core, nearly bringing you to your knees.
<br><br>

<span class="narration">
No rest for tired bones.<br>
I've walked this path alone.<br>
Hopes carved like river stone.<br><br>
</span>

Your legs are moving on their own.
<br><br>

<span class="narration">
Walk here with me, you'll see<br>
There lies a way to be<br>
One with the waiting sea.<br><br>
</span>

You stop. <<He>> stands, no longer playing, but continuing the song.
<br><br>

<span class="narration">
The river shifts its tide<br>
For our names, cast aside,<br>
Lay unspoken, brookside.<br><br>
</span>

<<He>> steps into the <<if Time.isBloodMoon()>>red<</if>> light. <<His>> face remains in the dark, but a <span class="tentacle">crackling antler</span> of sheer emptiness pokes free from the gloom. Moonlight reflects off of its three terrible prongs.
<br><br>

<span class="narration">
Hush now, return to sleep.<br>
The Elk, followed by sheep,<br>
Stole our black hearts to keep.<br><br>
</span>

The claws of an elongated, blackened arm stretch towards you, one pointing right over your heart. The spot where Avery was holding the dagger. It burns.
<br><br>

<<if $avery_mansion.fox.progress gte 5>>
	A creature you once knew the name stands before you.
<<else>>
	A creature with no name stares you down.
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<set $seabird_lullaby to 1>>

<<link [[Kneel|Mansion Piano Demon 2]]>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Apologise|Mansion Piano Demon 2]]>><<set $phase to 2>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Scream|Mansion Piano Demon 2]]>><<set $phase to 3>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Piano Demon 2
<<effects>>
<<if $phase is 1>>
	You slowly kneel. Its sharp fingers follow you down.
	<<if $demon gte 6>>
		You feel profoundly small. Your horns feel like nubs compared to its glorious crown of antlers. <span class="red">This is a true demon.</span>
	<<elseif $fallenangel gte 2>>
		You feel hollow, staring at an empty reflection of something so familiar. Like a cracked mirror.
	<<elseif $angel gte 6>>
		You feel humbled, brought low by something that is in every way your opposite.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	From the right side of its darkened face, a single green eye stares. It becomes more gentle, half-closing. Its hand gently grasps your shoulder, and pulls up. The command is clear. <span class="blue">Stand.</span>
	<br><br>

	You obey.
<<elseif $phase is 2>>
	You open your mouth, but no noise comes out. It understands, though.
	<br><br>

	Its head tilts curiously. From the right side of its darkened face, a single green eye stares. It becomes more gentle, half-closing.
<<else>>
	You open your mouth to scream, <span class="red">and only a faint mist escapes.</span> It flows forward, snaking around its fingers.
	<br><br>

	Its head tilts curiously. From the right side of its darkened face, a single green eye stares. It becomes more gentle, half-closing.
<</if>>
<br><br>

You hear the straining and stretching of sinew as its arm moves. It places its hand flat against your chest. <span class="purple">Your heartbeat grows louder.</span>
<br><br>

<<if $avery_mansion.fox.progress gte 5>>
	Its eye closes, and you hear something like a sigh of relief as it feels your heart. Its hand retracts back into the shadows.
<<else>>
	Its eye closes, satisfied by what it felt, and its hand retracts back into the shadows.
<</if>>
It turns away and walks towards the mask on the floor, exposing itself fully to the moon. Its skin shines, marked by countless old scars. All is dead silent.
<br><br>

It puts the mask on. Its head twitches.
<br><br>

Something that was once a person turns around. Its hand slowly points to you, then back to itself. Black sludge trickles from its eyes down the cheeks of its mask.
No words are shared, but you understand. There is no glory, no pleasure here. This is damnation.
<br><br>

It's a warning. This is the path you're treading.
<br><br>

It lumbers back into the shadows, away from the cruel light. It raises its hand to you and closes it. Your eyes close on their own.
<br><br>

When they open again, <<he>> is gone. Nobody is here.
<br><br>

<<set $avery_mansion.fox.end to true>>

<<link [[Next|Mansion Lounge]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Piano Fox 2
<<effects>><<summon_brown_fox 1>><<person1>>
You step into the <<if $avery_fate isnot "saved">>ruined<</if>> lounge doorway. A beam of <<if Time.isBloodMoon()>>red<</if>> moonlight lands just below the piano, revealing the end of a <<if $avery_mansion.fox.saved>><span class="blue">lightly burnt</span><</if>> dark green cloak.
A brown fox mask lies on the seat next to <<him>>.
<br><br>

<<if $avery_fate isnot "saved">>
	<<switch Weather.name>>
		<<case "lightPrecipitation" "heavyPrecipitation" "thunderStorm">>Enough of the upper structure is intact to give shelter from the <<= Weather.precipitation>>.
		<<default>>
	<</switch>>
<</if>>

<<if $avery_fate isnot "saved">>
	Despite the surrounding ash and ruin, the piano looks miraculously untouched.
<</if>>
With a flourish, <<he>> finishes the composition. <<He>> stands and turns to you, <<his>> face obscured by the darkness.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Mansion Piano Fox Talk]]>><<set $mansion_fox_followup to []>><<set $mansion_fox_talk to "intro">><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Piano Fox Talk
<<effects>>

<<switch $mansion_fox_talk>>
	<<case "intro">>"I'm sorry," <<he>> says.
	<<case "apology">>
		<<if !$mansion_fox_followup.includesAny("apologyAccept", "apologyDeny")>>
			<<His>> head tilts.
			<<if $mansion_fox_followup.includes("apologyAccept")>>
				"You accepted my apology without even knowing what it was for?" <<He>> giggles.
			<<else>>
				"You denied my apology without even knowing what it was for?" <<He>> pouts.
			<</if>>
		<</if>>
		"You weren't meant to be that close to the bones when they activated. You weren't meant to be in the tower at all. I know their rituals. The Silver Fox changed it. <<nnpc_He "Harper">> knew something."
		<br><br>

		<<He>> lets out a dry, sad laugh. "<<nnpc_Hes "Harper">> still one step ahead of everyone else."
		<br><br>

		<<He>> sits back down.
		<<if $avery_mansion.fox.friend>>
			"I had come to the mansion to watch the tower with you. Congratulate you on a job well done, and share a drink.
		<<else>>
			"I had come to the mansion to look for you.
		<</if>>
		When I didn't find you here, I ran to the tower as fast as I could.
		<<if $avery_mansion.fox.saved>>
			I'm glad I made it to you in time."
		<<elseif $avery_fate is "saved">>
			You didn't need my help, though." <<He>> leans forward into the light just enough for you to see <<his>> smile. "Your flight was beautiful, dear."
		<<else>>
			I feared the worst."
		<</if>>
		<<if $avery_mansion.fox.friend>>
			<<set $mansion_fox_followup.pushUnique("can_drink")>>
			<br><br>
			You hear something slide against the top of the piano.
			<<if !(playerIsPregnant() and playerAwareTheyArePregnant())>>
				Moonlight reflects off of two wine glasses, and a bottle of wine. "I keep my promises."
			<<else>>
				Moonlight reflects off of two wine glasses, a bottle of wine, and a bottle of sparkling grape juice. "I keep my promises."
			<</if>>
		<</if>>
	<<case "apologyAccept">>
		<<He>> smiles and bows. "Your heart is a kind one."
	<<case "apologyDeny">>
		<<He>> frowns and nods. "As is your right. I failed in my part, and it cost you dearly. I only hope that, one day, you'll find it in your heart to forgive me."
	<<case "drink">>
		<<set $avery_mansion.fox.drink to true>>
		<<if !$mansion_fox_followup.includes("mask")>>
			<<set $mansion_fox_followup.pushUnique("mask")>>
			<<He>> dons <<his>> mask and steps into the light.
		<</if>>
		<<He>> pours your drinks.
		<<if $avery_fate is "saved">>
			The two of you cheer, your glasses clinking together just a little louder than you had intended. You both wince, looking up the stairs towards the bedroom. No noise comes from it. The brown fox giggles, and you drink.
		<<else>>
			The two of you cheer, your glasses clinking together. You drink.
		<</if>>
		<br><br>

		<<He>> lets out a satisfied huff after downing <<his>> glass. "It tastes so much better with a partner, doesn't it?" <<note "+ ???" "green">>
	<<case "bonesReal">>
		<<if !$mansion_fox_followup.includes("bonesFake")>>
			"I suppose I owe you answers. I don't normally speak so freely." <<He>> paces.
		<</if>>
		"They're wrist bones. That's why they're called 'clutching bones.' They're very old. Preserved as a holy relic. Or an unholy one, depending on who you ask."
		<br><br>

		<<He>> turns to you. "Hold on to them. You're their keeper, now."
	<<case "bonesFake">>
		<<if !$mansion_fox_followup.includes("bonesReal")>>
			"I suppose I owe you answers. I don't normally speak so freely." <<He>> paces.
		<</if>>
		"They were the bones of a deceased whale, picked clean. It gave life to those at the bottom. It takes life back from those at the top just as easily."
		<br><br>

		<<He>> folds <<his>> hands in front of <<him>>. "I hollowed them out, and carved them into shape from photos that Landry had of the real ones. The rest was simple chemistry." <<His>> explanation is cold and clinical, lacking any sort of pride or emotion.
	<<case "thank">>
		<<He>> looks away. "It was my fault you were in that position to begin with. I don't deserve your thanks.
		<<if $avery_fate is "saved">>
			You alone saved Avery. No one else could have." <<He>> pauses. "And I don't think anyone else would have, if given the same choice. You are so... so very curious."
		<<else>>
			You saved yourself."
		<</if>>
	<<case "thank_how">>
		"I'm not sure what you mean. All I did was push you out of the way, and help you out of the debris."
	<<case "thank_saw">>
		<<He>> doesn't respond.
	<<case "AveryMad">>
		<<He>> looks down. "I'm sorry. The High Elk was the primary target, or so I thought. We inflicted a wound, but the outcome was... not as intended."
		<<He>> looks up to the moon. "Our conflict has only just begun. I hope you stay clear of it. You've done so much already. More than you know."
	<<case "Avery">>
		<<He>> looks down. "I did. The High Elk was the primary target, or so I thought."
		<br><br>
		<<if $avery_fate is "saved">>
			<<He>> lets out a long breath. "Perhaps, someday, redemption will find Avery." <<He>> looks up to the moon. "Our conflict has only just begun.
		<<else>>
			<<He>> lets out a long breath. "In a way, Avery is saved. Saved from something worse. What happened was a mercy. Weep not for the fallen." <<He>> looks up to the moon. "Our conflict has only just begun. Mourning must wait until the end.
		<</if>>
		I hope you stay clear of it. You've done so much already. More than you know."
	<<case "help">>
		<<He>> doesn't respond at first, only looking down and covering <<his>> mouth.
		<<if !$mansion_fox_followup.includes("mask")>>
			<<set $mansion_fox_followup.pushUnique("mask")>>
			<<He>> dons <<his>> mask and steps into the light.
		<<else>>
			<<He>> steps into the light.
		<</if>>
		<br><br>

		"Oh, my dear child." <<He>> hugs you. "You must have had a hard life, to give of yourself so willingly." <<He>> pulls back, smiling.
		"I'm still not used to working with others, but perhaps I've worked alone for too long. <span class="green">Some day soon, we will again.</span> I promise."
	<<case "mask">>
		You try to get a closer look at <<his>> face. Every time you do, it seems as though a cloud blocks the light of the moon just enough to obscure it.
		<br><br>

		"You're just going to give yourself eye strain doing that, dear." <<He>> dons <<his>> mask.
	<<case "piano">>
		"You know the melody, don't you?" <<He>> smiles. "Perhaps I'll share the words with you, some day."
	<<case "flirt">>
		<<set $seductiondifficulty to 8000>>
		<<seductioncheck>>
		<<seductionskilluptext>>
		<<seductionskilluse>>
		<<promiscuity1>>

		<<if $seductionrating gte $seductionrequired>>
			<<set $avery_mansion.fox.flirt to true>>
			<<He>> giggles.
			<<if $avery_fate is "saved">>
				"I don't think Avery would like that very much."
				<<He>> leans in. "Perhaps I'll sneak in some day while <<nnpc_hes "Avery">> away." <<He>> places a finger under your chin. "Or maybe you should keep such thoughts to yourself." <<He>> smiles sweetly. <<glust>>
			<<else>>
				"I suppose you're open now that Avery's gone, aren't you?"
				<<He>> leans in. "Perhaps I'll come find you sooner that anticipated, for pleasure before business." <<He>> places a finger under your chin. "Or maybe you should keep such thoughts to yourself." <<He>> smiles sweetly. <<glust>>
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			<<He>> giggles. "I'm flattered, dear, but I'm far too much for you."
		<</if>>
	<<case "leave">>
		<<if !$mansion_fox_followup.includes("mask")>>
			<<set $mansion_fox_followup.pushUnique("mask")>>
			<<He>> dons <<his>> mask.
		<</if>>
		"How rude, not even saying hello."
		<br><br>

		<<He>> kicks off of the piano and lands right in front of you, <<his>> face still obscured by shadows. <<He>> places a finger under your chin. "Be a good <<girl>> and smell the roses, won't you?"
		<br><br>

		You try to move around <<him>>, but <<he>> keeps leaning in your way. You don't have much choice but to stay, for now.
	<<default>><<He>> sneezes cutely.
<</switch>>
<<set $mansion_fox_followup.pushUnique($mansion_fox_talk)>>
<br><br>

<<if !$mansion_fox_followup.includes("apology")>>
	<<link [[Ask what <<hes>> sorry for|Mansion Piano Fox Talk]]>><<set $mansion_fox_talk to "apology">><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if !$mansion_fox_followup.includesAny("apologyAccept", "apologyDeny")>>
	<<link [[Accept apology|Mansion Piano Fox Talk]]>><<set $mansion_fox_talk to "apologyAccept">><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Deny apology|Mansion Piano Fox Talk]]>><<set $mansion_fox_talk to "apologyDeny">><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if $mansion_fox_followup.includes("apology") and !$mansion_fox_followup.includes("bonesReal") and !$avery_mansion.fox.bones>>
	<<link [[Ask what the wishing stones really are|Mansion Piano Fox Talk]]>><<set $mansion_fox_talk to "bonesReal">><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if $mansion_fox_followup.includes("apology") and !$mansion_fox_followup.includes("bonesFake") and !$avery_mansion.fox.bones>>
	<<link [[Ask what the fake stones really were|Mansion Piano Fox Talk]]>><<set $mansion_fox_talk to "bonesFake">><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if $mansion_fox_followup.includes("can_drink") and !$mansion_fox_followup.includes("drink")>>
	<<if !(playerIsPregnant() and playerAwareTheyArePregnant())>>
		<<link [[Drink with <<him>>|Mansion Piano Fox Talk]]>><<set $mansion_fox_talk to "drink">><</link>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		<<link [[Drink with <<him>>|Mansion Piano Fox Talk]]>><<set $mansion_fox_talk to "drink">><<alcohol 60>><</link>><<galcohol>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<<if $avery_mansion.fox.saved>>
	<<if !$mansion_fox_followup.includes("thank")>>
		<<if $avery_fate is "saved">>
			<<link [[Thank <<him>> for saving you and Avery|Mansion Piano Fox Talk]]>><<set $mansion_fox_talk to "thank">><</link>>
			<br>
		<<else>>
			<<link [[Thank <<him>> for saving you|Mansion Piano Fox Talk]]>><<set $mansion_fox_talk to "thank">><</link>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
	<<elseif $mansion_fox_followup.includes("thank") and !$mansion_fox_followup.includes("thank_how")>>
		<<link [[Ask how <<he>> saved you|Mansion Piano Fox Talk]]>><<set $mansion_fox_talk to "thank_how">><</link>>
		<br>
	<<elseif $mansion_fox_followup.includes("thank_how") and !$mansion_fox_followup.includes("thank_saw")>>
		<<link [[Say you never saw <<him>> escape|Mansion Piano Fox Talk]]>><<set $mansion_fox_talk to "thank_saw">><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<<if !$mansion_fox_followup.includesAny("Avery", "AveryMad")>>
	<<if $avery_fate is "saved">>
		<<link [[Get angry about <<his>> idea of 'saving' Avery|Mansion Piano Fox Talk]]>><<set $mansion_fox_talk to "AveryMad">><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<link [[Say you thought <<he>> wanted to save Avery|Mansion Piano Fox Talk]]>><<set $mansion_fox_talk to "Avery">><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if $mansion_fox_followup.includesAny("Avery", "AveryMad") and !$mansion_fox_followup.includes("help")>>
	<<link [[Say you'll help however you can|Mansion Piano Fox Talk]]>><<set $mansion_fox_talk to "help">><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if !$mansion_fox_followup.includes("mask")>>
	<<link [[Try to get a better look at <<his>> face|Mansion Piano Fox Talk]]>><<set $mansion_fox_talk to "mask">><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if !$mansion_fox_followup.includes("piano")>>
	<<link [[Ask <<him>> about the song <<he>> was playing|Mansion Piano Fox Talk]]>><<set $mansion_fox_talk to "piano">><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if $mansion_fox_followup.includes("drink") and !$mansion_fox_followup.includes("flirt")>>
	<<link [[Flirt|Mansion Piano Fox Talk]]>><<set $mansion_fox_talk to "flirt">><</link>><<promiscuous1>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<br>

<<if $mansion_fox_followup.includesAny("apologyAccept", "apologyDeny")>>
	<<link [[Say goodbye to the brown fox|Mansion Piano Fox Talk End]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<if $avery_mansion.fox.friend or $mansion_fox_followup.includes("help")>>
		<<link [[Say goodbye, and that you hope to meet again soon|Mansion Piano Fox Talk End]]>><<set $mansion_fox_talk to "soon">><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<if !$mansion_fox_followup.includes("help")>>
		<<link [[Say you hope you never have to meet each other again|Mansion Piano Fox Talk End]]>><<set $mansion_fox_talk to "never">><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<<elseif !$mansion_fox_followup.includes("leave")>>
	<<link [[Just leave|Mansion Piano Fox Talk End]]>><<set $mansion_fox_talk to "leave">><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Mansion Piano Fox Talk End
<<effects>>
<<if $mansion_fox_followup.includes("can_drink") and !$mansion_fox_followup.includes("drink")>>
	<<He>> frowns, sliding the wine and glasses back into the shadows.
<</if>>
<<if !$mansion_fox_followup.includes("mask")>>
	<<He>> dons <<his>> mask.
<</if>>
<<if $mansion_fox_talk is "soon">>
	"It may be sooner than you think.
<<elseif $mansion_fox_talk is "never">>
	"I'm afraid I have no control over that, my dear.
<<else>>
	"Until we meet again.
<</if>>
May your triumphs and troubles shape you into diamond."
<br><br>

<<He>> brushes by you, and vanishes into the night.
<<unset $mansion_fox_followup>><<unset $mansion_fox_talk>>
<<set $avery_mansion.fox.end to true>>
<br><br>

